# Every world `two_disk_hanoi.trig` forked, in the order the search made them — 14 of them.
# Regenerated by `pytest packages/orexis-agent-deliberation/tests --update-snapshots`; review the diff, it is the claim.

# two_disk_hanoi
#
# WHAT ONE ITERATION OF THE SEARCH DOES, on the smallest problem that has more than one answer.
#
# Two disks on three pegs: nine states, three moves to solve. The small disk sits on the big
# one, the big one on peg A, and every disk must end on peg C.
#
# An ITERATION takes one node off the open list and forks a world per lever the node's own
# world affords — here the small disk is the only movable one, and it may go to B or to C, so
# the first iteration makes TWO worlds and not one. Each is a NAMED GRAPH in the imaginarium,
# named for how it was reached, and holds only that node's own readings: what the move added
# and what it retracted, never a copy of the world. `<case>.worlds.trig` beside this file is
# every world forked, in the order they were made.
#
# THE WORLDS DO NOT SURVIVE THE PASS. A node's graph is dropped once it is expanded and again
# when the pass ends, to be re-made from the nearest kept graph when a rule next runs against
# it — so a snapshot of the store afterwards shows none of this, which is why they are caught
# as they are made.
#
# THE PUZZLE IS THE DOMAIN'S, NOT THIS FILE'S. `hanoi:Move`, `hanoi:solved` and
# `hanoi:disksAstray` are copied verbatim from `packages/orexis-tool-hanoi/`, because a case
# loads no package — and their rule texts speak `hanoi:`, a name the store discovered from that
# package's own ontology, so they survive the rewrite a locally-declared prefix would not.
#
# The clock stands at 2026-01-01T12:00:00Z.

@prefix : <http://example.org/test#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix deliberation: <http://example.org/orexis/deliberation#> .
@prefix progression: <http://example.org/orexis/progression#> .
@prefix hanoi: <http://example.org/orexis/hanoi#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix graph: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/> .
#  Where a forked world lands. Nothing in the case says this graph; the imaginarium
#  names each world it makes, and the prefix is here so `<case>.worlds.trig` reads.
@prefix possible: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/possible/> .
@prefix pursued: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/pursued/keeper/> .


#  1. from sensed
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  2. from sensed
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  3. from Move-disk_1-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_1-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on :disk_2 .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  4. from Move-disk_1-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_1-PegB {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  5. from Move-disk_1-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
}

#  6. from Move-disk_1-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_1-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on :disk_2 .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  7. from Move-disk_1-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_1-PegC {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  8. from Move-disk_1-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
}

#  9. from Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  10. from Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB.Move-disk_1-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
}

#  11. from Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegB.Move-disk_1-PegB {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on :disk_2 .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
}

#  12. from Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC.Move-disk_2-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegB .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
}

#  13. from Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC.Move-disk_1-PegA {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on hanoi:PegA .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
}

#  14. from Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC
GRAPH possible:Move-disk_1-PegB.Move-disk_2-PegC.Move-disk_1-PegC {
  :disk_1 hanoi:on :disk_2 .
  :disk_2 hanoi:on hanoi:PegC .
}

